{{#if programLibrary}}
### Reusing a program you already ran

gg keeps the source of every program you run. `{{api.programs.get.call}}(turn)` takes an
optional turn number: pass nothing for the last program you ran, or a number for
the one from that turn. `{{api.programs.history.call}}()` lists the turns it still holds.

Use this when a program was nearly right. Fetch it, patch it as a `std::string`,
and hand it back with `{{api.programs.rerun.call}}(source)` — gg runs what you hand over as
this turn's program, so a one-character fix costs one line instead of the whole
program again:

```cpp
int main() {
  std::string source = {{api.programs.get.call}}();
  const auto at = source.find("int totl = 1");
  if (at != std::string::npos) source.replace(at, 12, "int total = 1");
  {{api.programs.rerun.call}}(source);
  return 0;
}
```

Everything the handing-over program already did stands, so hand over before
doing work you do not want done twice. Hand over once per turn: the first
hand-over is the one that runs.
{{/if}}

