{{#if skills}}
## Skills

You have skills available — short guides, and in some cases reusable **code**,
for parts of this task. Read one with `{{api.skills.read_skill.call}}(name)`. These are the
skills you have:

{{#each skills}}
- `{{name}}` — {{description}}
{{/each}}

Reading a skill does up to three things, and the reply tells you which:

- its prose is pinned into your context for the rest of the session, including
  across a compaction;
- if it carries code, that code is bound at `lib::<key>` for every program you
  write from then on — the reply names the key and what it exports. It is
  compiled into the same artifact as your program, so `lib::<key>::<name>(args…)`
  is an ordinary qualified call the compiler checks: a key or a name that does
  not exist is a diagnostic rather than a surprise, and the default arguments the
  skill's author wrote are the ones you get;
- if it carries an on-use script, gg runs it once your program has ended, so
  whatever it shows you arrives on your next turn.

{{/if}}

